jobs.description:
Are you ready to pick the perfect job? 🤔 This is your dream job as a warehouse worker at Wasco. 📦 As a warehouse worker at Wasco in Apeldoorn you can earn up to €20,26 per hour. So, grab this opportunity to become the best orderpicker from Wasco! 🚀

For this function you will need your own housing in the Netherlands. Unfortunately we do not offer housing with this job. ❌ Apply now and get a WhatsApp message within 15 minutes with questions so we can help you quickly. 📱 Do not have a WhatsApp? 📞 Then we will contact you by phone or email! ✉️

What we offer
- Great salary! Starting from €16,21 per hour (21+)
- Allowances up to 25%! That means €20,26 per hour!
- Working full-time or part-time during the week! 💪
- Every weekend you are free, nice! 📝
- Opportunities to develop and learn!
- A really nice and fun work environment!

Who you are
To keep the warehouse running smoothly, it is important that you meet the following requirements:

-     You speak English, for safety reasons;    
- You are at least 18 years old, due to driving an EPT;    
- You are at least available to work on Mondays and Fridays (more days are possible);    
- You are available to work in different shifts. The working hours are from 09:00 to 18:00 and  12:00 to 21:00;    
- You have your own transport to get to Apeldoorn;    
- You are physically capable of lifting product weighing at least 20 kilos;    
- You agree that we can not offer a guarantee of hours.

What will you do
Let me take you through a typical workday as a warehouse worker at Wasco in Apeldoorn! When you arrive at the warehouse, you start your day with a free cup of coffee. ☕ Then you lace up your work shoes. You step into the spacious warehouse and greet your friendly colleagues. You will be working with a voice pick system, where orders are sent straight to your headset. 🎧 You will locate the products in the warehouse. And lift them onto your EPT to transport them to their designated spots. Expect to work with heavy items like toilet bow

As an operator, you'll work in a two-shift system and be responsible for part of the production process. By operating the machines, your goal is to meet production demand with the desired quality. Independently operate, monitor, and maintain the production line;

- Identify and resolve machine malfunctions;
- Set up machines based on the production schedule;
- Monitor product quality using various measuring instruments;
- Ensure timely machine maintenance in consultation with your manager and the Technical Department;
- Contribute to structural improvement opportunities;
- Coordinating workflows in consultation with your manager.

- A technical background or extensive experience in production technology is a plus;
- You are willing to work night shifts;
- You have technical knowledge and enjoy brainstorming;
- You are a natural at solution-oriented error analysis;
- You are a precision engineer;
- You have knowledge of and experience with production processes;
- You are decisive, practical, and enjoy working in a team.
- A driving license (car) is preferred - Maintec arranges transport;
- You can communicate in English at a B1/B2 level.

As an Electrical Panel Technician, you will be responsible for assembling, wiring, and testing electrical control cabinets and operating panels. You will work from electrical schematics and technical drawings to ensure all systems are built according to the required specifications and quality standards.

Your main responsibilities include:

- Reading and interpreting electrical drawings and diagrams;
- Mounting electrical components and hardware;
- Wiring and assembling control cabinets and panels;
- Testing and inspecting completed systems before delivery;
- Supporting installation or commissioning work when needed.
- Most of your activities will take place in the workshop, with occasional on-site assignments at customer locations.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with panel building or electrical assembly work is preferred;
- Ability to read and understand electrical schematics;
- Accurate and independent working attitude;
- Team player with a hands-on mentality;
- Good command of English (Dutch is an advantage).

As a Maritime Electrical Technician, you will work on the installation, maintenance, and repair of electrical systems on different types of vessels, including yachts, offshore vessels, and workboats. You will be involved in projects ranging from new shipbuilding to maintenance and refit activities.

Your responsibilities include:

- Reading and interpreting maritime electrical drawings and schematics;
- Installing onboard cabling, switchboards, and control systems;
- Testing and commissioning electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Supporting upgrades and modifications of onboard systems.

You will mainly work at shipyards and port locations, with occasional assignments on board vessels.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or Maritime Technology;
- Experience with electrical installations, preferably in the maritime sector;
- Knowledge of maritime systems and standards is an advantage;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Independent and accurate working style;
- Good command of Dutch or English.

As a Shipboard Electrician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical systems onboard ships and maritime installations. You will work with a variety of systems, including power distribution, lighting, navigation equipment, automation systems, and communication networks.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting electrical systems onboard vessels;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Inspecting, testing, and commissioning maritime electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing maintenance and repair activities on onboard systems;
- Supporting refit, modernization, and new-build projects.

You will primarily work at shipyards, ports, and onboard vessels, with occasional travel required for project support and sea trials.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related technical field;
- Relevant experience as an electrician, preferably within shipbuilding, maritime, or offshore environments;
- Knowledge of maritime electrical systems and regulations is an advantage;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Flexible, proactive, and solution-oriented attitude;
- Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English.

As an Industrial Service Electrician, you will perform installation, maintenance, and repair work on industrial electrical systems. You will work on projects involving machinery, control cabinets, cable systems, and power installations. Safety and quality are essential in your daily work.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing industrial cabling and electrical components;
- Maintaining and testing electrical systems;
- Analyzing and solving technical faults;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings;
- Supporting project teams during installation activities.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with industrial electrical installations;
- VCA certification is preferred;
- Knowledge of industrial safety standards is an advantage;
- Flexible and hands-on mentality;
- Good command of Dutch or English.
